Expected elements: present

The provenance marker is present as the `Data` row at the head of the Overview grid, badge and capture sentences together, and it is the only one of the three forms on the page — the absent band is the change, not a gap. `Not observable`, the published pruning reason, the permanence claim, the full hash, the outcome badge, the four facts, all content sections in the permanent tense, nav, footer, disclosure and provenance strip are present, and nothing forbidden appears.

The single weakest element is the note card in the **Decoded input** section, immediately below the `SELECTOR / RAW` grid. It reads: "This selector is not in any ABI BlockTracer holds, so the parameters are shown as raw bytes. Supplying an ABI decodes them." The two rows it explains say `SELECTOR —` and `RAW 0x`. There is no selector. There are no parameters. No raw bytes are shown. And the page's own raw block, 1,300px lower, gives the real reason: `"bodyRetainedAtCapture": false`. The body was pruned — the same fact this page states twice, carefully, elsewhere.

It is the weakest because it is the only element on a page built entirely to be honest about what cannot be known that says something untrue, blames this product's ABI holdings for the chain's retention policy, and hands the reader an action ("Supplying an ABI decodes them") that cannot work. Every other empty section on this page names its true, permanent reason. This one does not.

